From 07d10274a78d88022db9524d7e661b2a6367b71d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:53:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(face): do not lift over a hole that is below the cut
 plane

A Face on a model source read each hole of the part's silhouette as a
hole of the face. A through-hole in a low flange was lifted over also
when the cut plane was above the hole's rim. The row ends beside the
lift stood within a tool radius of the open outer rim, and verify
reported each one as a gouge.

Under FaceHoles::Lift the Face arm now passes the outline of the
material at or above the cut plane (material_source::standing_at).
face_holes::beside bridges a hole only when that material stands in it
or beside it. A boss, and a bore whose rim the plane reaches, are
lifted over as before. CutAir and Through do not change.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/face_holes_below_cut.rs and
face_holes::law::lift_bridges_only_the_holes_that_material_at_the_plane_touches.

Fixes #2437

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
